{"kind":"charness.bounded_review.v1","lens":"release lock-in final pass","verdict":"block","target_observations":null,"findings":[{"id":"R-005","severity":"low","summary":"The reported R-004 sequence is corrected, but the operator guide’s unconditional post-delivery stop claim omits a case that can delay stopping by another check: a new command started since the previous check is still young. The `ProgressRule` class docstring repeats that oversimplification.","evidence":["docs/agent-task-runs.md: “the next empty check after delivery stops it.”","scripts/task_run/task_run_progress_rule.py: the `ProgressRule` docstring says a delivered request means “the next empty check stops the lane.”","charness-artifacts/spec/lane-progress-rule.md: a command started since the previous check can defer “the request, or the stop” until completion or the next check.","tests/charness_cli/test_task_run_progress_rule.py: `test_a_command_started_after_the_request_is_not_killed_until_it_is_a_window_old` covers a young command after request delivery."],"action":"Qualify the guide and class docstring: a young command can defer either request delivery or stopping by one check; otherwise, the next empty check after delivery stops the lane."}],"counterweight_triage":[{"concern":"R-003: readers could take the progress windows as a hard wall-clock bound.","bin":"fixed","disposition":"The spec and release notes call windows nominal and explicitly disclaim a hard wall-clock bound; no closed-form bound is needed."},{"concern":"R-004: the request and stop sequence after a young command was described one check too early.","bin":"fixed for the reported sequence","disposition":"The guide now says the request is delivered a check later when the command is young, with stopping after delivery; the separate post-delivery young-command case is captured in R-005."}],"next_move":"Clarify the additional young-command exception in the guide and class docstring, then repeat the bounded review.","non_claims":["Reviewed the 17 identity-bound inline files only; did not inspect workspace paths, run tests, or independently verify live runtime behavior."]}
